WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.362
Where are agencies?

2
00:00:01.362 --> 00:00:04.461
In commercial Azure,
which a G C C tenant uses,

3
00:00:04.461 --> 00:00:07.301
everything in this module is available.

4
00:00:07.301 --> 00:00:09.265
As a side note for Azure Government:

5
00:00:09.265 --> 00:00:13.873
Learn's frequently asked questions for
the Application Gateway firewall say it's

6
00:00:13.873 --> 00:00:15.635
supported in sovereign clouds,

7
00:00:15.635 --> 00:00:19.362
but geo-filtering custom rules and
bot protection rule sets aren't.

8
00:00:19.362 --> 00:00:24.569
So leave the bot manager rule set out, and
record that Zero Trust test as skipped,

9
00:00:24.569 --> 00:00:28.013
not applicable, for the
environment, not as a failure.

10
00:00:28.013 --> 00:00:31.672
Front Door's own sovereign-cloud
limits aren't yet specified;

11
00:00:31.672 --> 00:00:36.137
assume the Application Gateway ones
until a test policy shows otherwise.

12
00:00:36.137 --> 00:00:40.736
DDoS Protection has no variation
listed, but which simulation partners

13
00:00:40.736 --> 00:00:45.488
serve Azure Government isn't specified,
and Red Button is public cloud only.

14
00:00:45.488 --> 00:00:51.808
On other clouds, the guide names AWS
Shield and AWS W A F, Google Cloud Armor,

15
00:00:51.808 --> 00:00:57.287
and O C I W A F as a regional policy
on a load balancer or at the edge.

16
00:00:57.287 --> 00:01:01.680
DDoS protection on Oracle Cloud
Infrastructure isn't compared there.
